Z||000004||fiero56||10-19-2001||06:56 AM||||'88 exhaust tips are different length than previous years. Been there, done that. Stand both tips side by side on the ground on megaphone end. If the bend is the same height on both sides, they are '88, if one is 1" higher, they are pre'88 and won't fit/look right.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||10-19-2001||09:32 AM||||Well, CRAP!  I hadn't noticed that.  Mine are off of an 85.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  The passenger side pipe is bent, so I'd have to get the fixed anyway.  Maybe the muffler shop can take care of that and the length at the same time?<P>If anyone's already done it, I'd love to see pics!||||reg||9
Z||000006||RossT||10-19-2001||09:38 AM||||I double crap what he just said!!  Now I have to find the tips from an 88 to fit my<BR>formula.  That will make it that much harder.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Philphine||10-19-2001||11:12 AM||||wait a minute. if i understood the explaination of the difference you can alter them if they are off the car, i think.<P> i just cut the megaphone part off my gt exhaust and left the pipe that came through them intact. mine just had two tack welds holding each megaphone on. if you have the tips off so you can get to both sides good you might be able to grind the tack welds off, slide the megaphone to the right lenght and tack them back. the altering should be far enough under the car to not be very notisable.<P>they need to be off the car though. mine were on so i could only get to the bottom weld, so i pretty much slit the megaphones down the bottom with the grinder (destroyed them), split them open and broke the top weld off. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||10-19-2001||12:15 PM||||I was thinking about that.  It does look like the GT tips are just megaphones slid over the regular tips.  If that's the case, I should be able to grind off the welds and have the megs tacked onto my Formula's factory tips.  I'll check into that this weekend, if I can.||||reg||6
Z||000009||88CoupeV6||10-19-2001||01:57 PM||||I have the Megs from an 86 SE on mine. I used the entire exhaust system from the y pipe back. I think it looks fine.<P>Here is <B>a real old pic</B> of my car from the back. It shows the tips<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mar19^05_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Philphine||10-19-2001||04:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>I was thinking about that.  It does look like the GT tips are just megaphones slid over the regular tips.  If that's the case, I should be able to grind off the welds and have the megs tacked onto my Formula's factory tips.  I'll check into that this weekend, if I can.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>formula, before you try that measure and see how far apart the outlets are on your formula. it seemed like on my '87 coupe since it had no megs the pipes were closer together. i remember trying to put a tip on each end and they were too close for me to do it. if so the megaphones may not have room to sit side by side. it may not be a problem but it won't hurt to check first.||||reg||1
